S
#28703
The Lagoon~
Tiny fish tickle your navel as you swim into the ever-deepening lagoon.
Brain coral has established itself in large islands, and the ripples in
the sand at the bottom of the lagoon cast strange striped shadows which
remind you of fine Elven cloth.  You look up just in time to realize that
you are being carried out to sea through a narrow channel by a strong
current.~
287 0 SECT_WATER_SWIM
DDIR_NORTH
~
~
0 -1 28705
DDIR_WEST
~
~
0 -1 28701
S
#28704
The Narrow Channel~
Sand-covered coral crops out on both sides as the powerful current carries
you relentlessly out to sea.  Sea urchins cling tenously just below the
surface of the water, and schools of larger fish feed on nutrients carried
from the lagoon.~
287 0 SECT_WATER_SWIM
DDIR_NORTH
~
~
0 -1 28707
DDIR_SOUTH
~
~
0 -1 28702
S
#28705
The Narrow Channel~
The water sweeps you past a row of small breakers which threaten to spear
you on the spines of the large urchins clinging to the rocks in this hostile
setting.  High spires of dead coral rise above you on either side, and the
deep blue sea extends all the way to the northern horizon.~
287 0 SECT_WATER_SWIM
DDIR_NORTH
~
~
0 -1 28708
DDIR_SOUTH
~
~
0 -1 28703
S
#28706
Atop the Barrier Island~
You have climbed up on a sandy island which seperates the lagoon from the
deep blue sea to the north.  A huge line of breakers, three or four
whitecaps deep, speak of dangerous undertow and riptides that would make
travel to the north unadvisable.  As you turn to return the way you came,
you notice a small shack constructed of driftwood.~
287 0 SECT_DESERT
DDIR_SOUTH
~
~
